<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">March First Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Samil Movement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The March First Movement was a nationwide Korean protest against Japanese colonial rule that began on 1 March 1919 with the reading of a Declaration of Independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a>. Hundreds of thousands joined peaceful demonstrations, which the Japanese authorities suppressed with thousands of deaths. It led to the founding of the Provisional Government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">Republic of Korea</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/march-first-movement.jpg" alt="March First Movement" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bureau d'information coréen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%E2%80%99Ind%C3%A9pendance_de_la_Cor%C3%A9e_et_la_Paix-02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
